1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,460
Hello everyone and welcome to EnglishPod.

2
00:00:05,780 --> 00:00:06,340
My name is Marco.

3
00:00:06,860 --> 00:00:12,080
And my name is Catherine and today we've got a great lesson for you about traveling and getting directions.

4
00:00:12,740 --> 00:00:13,220
That's right.

5
00:00:13,500 --> 00:00:19,740
So sometimes we are looking for an address, we are looking for our friend's house and we can't find it.

6
00:00:19,860 --> 00:00:20,620
So what do you have to do?

7
00:00:20,840 --> 00:00:23,480
You have to stop and ask someone for directions.

8
00:00:23,900 --> 00:00:28,300
There's actually a joke in many countries that men hate to ask for directions.

9
00:00:29,180 --> 00:00:34,720
And so this is the women's approach, asking and getting directions and finally finding your way.

10
00:00:34,960 --> 00:00:36,120
So it's a good thing.

11
00:00:36,340 --> 00:00:37,320
That's a very good thing.

12
00:00:37,880 --> 00:00:40,280
So we're going to jump right into the dialogue.

13
00:00:40,280 --> 00:00:43,640
Let's see what happens here and if they can find the place they're looking for.

14
00:00:49,920 --> 00:00:52,030
We've been going around in circles for the past hour.

15
00:00:52,040 --> 00:00:55,180
Will you just please stop and ask for directions?

16
00:00:55,180 --> 00:00:56,150
We are not lost.

17
00:00:56,600 --> 00:00:57,890
I'm just taking the scenic route.

18
00:00:58,230 --> 00:00:58,810
Yeah, whatever.

19
00:00:59,390 --> 00:01:01,750
I told you we should buy that GPS that was on sale.

20
00:01:02,270 --> 00:01:03,090
But would you listen to me?

21
00:01:03,310 --> 00:01:05,050
No, this is so typical.

22
00:01:05,530 --> 00:01:05,870
Fine.

23
00:01:06,590 --> 00:01:09,450
I'll ask this guy for directions if it will shut your trap.

24
00:01:10,230 --> 00:01:11,010
Excuse me, sir.

25
00:01:11,290 --> 00:01:13,710
Can you tell me how to get to St. Mary's Church?

26
00:01:14,490 --> 00:01:15,010
Sure.

27
00:01:15,530 --> 00:01:23,090
Go down Park Road, turn left, go up as far as the set of traffic lights and turn left.

28
00:01:23,670 --> 00:01:26,730
The place you're looking for is the second building on the right.

29
00:01:27,370 --> 00:01:27,810
Thanks.

30
00:01:28,680 --> 00:01:30,080
See, was that hard?

31
00:01:30,500 --> 00:01:33,100
If you would only listen to me more often, you'd be better off.

32
00:01:34,160 --> 00:01:38,560
All right, we're back.

33
00:01:38,560 --> 00:01:44,110
So well, the woman was obviously a little bit angry that the guy refused to admit that he was lost.

34
00:01:44,640 --> 00:01:45,160
That's right.

35
00:01:45,380 --> 00:01:46,040
She's very frustrated.

36
00:01:46,600 --> 00:01:50,280
And this has been in movies and in books and all sorts of things.

37
00:01:50,720 --> 00:01:53,400
This kind of story of the man not wanting to ask for directions.

38
00:01:54,240 --> 00:01:58,480
And so he keeps saying, listen, I've got these excuses.

39
00:01:58,600 --> 00:02:00,300
I'm taking the scenic route, for example.

40
00:02:00,680 --> 00:02:01,240
That's right.

41
00:02:01,480 --> 00:02:04,980
And that's our first word for today on Language Takeaway.

42
00:02:06,630 --> 00:02:07,890
Language Takeaway.

43
00:02:08,650 --> 00:02:11,650
So as you say, the scenic route, what does he mean by that?

44
00:02:11,870 --> 00:02:16,650
Okay, route is like a path or a trail or kind of like the way that you go somewhere.

45
00:02:17,070 --> 00:02:18,310
So the route to my house.

46
00:02:18,920 --> 00:02:25,800
But in this case, the scenic route or the scenic route, you can say in both ways, is the most beautiful way to go.

47
00:02:25,800 --> 00:02:28,280
It's usually the longer one.

48
00:02:28,280 --> 00:02:29,280
Yeah.

49
00:02:29,280 --> 00:02:31,200
So you can say, oh, it's just the scenic route.

50
00:02:31,200 --> 00:02:31,910
It's not really true.

51
00:02:32,200 --> 00:02:33,390
It's just the longer route.

52
00:02:33,510 --> 00:02:34,170
Right, exactly.

53
00:02:34,960 --> 00:02:36,720
So that's the excuse that he's giving her.

54
00:02:36,720 --> 00:02:37,690
He's like, no, I'm not lost.

55
00:02:37,930 --> 00:02:41,150
We're taking longer because, well, we're taking the beautiful route.

56
00:02:41,610 --> 00:02:43,730
All right, with all the trees and the animals and the lakes.

57
00:02:44,080 --> 00:02:44,450
No, I don't.

58
00:02:45,080 --> 00:02:45,210
I don't buy it.

59
00:02:46,080 --> 00:02:47,080
I don't believe this.

60
00:02:47,080 --> 00:02:48,080
That's right.

61
00:02:48,080 --> 00:02:49,080
I don't believe it.

62
00:02:49,080 --> 00:02:50,080
I don't believe it.

63
00:02:50,080 --> 00:02:51,080
Whatever.

64
00:02:51,080 --> 00:02:52,080
You know what?

65
00:02:52,080 --> 00:02:53,080
We need a GPS.

66
00:02:53,080 --> 00:02:55,080
Okay, GPS, global positioning system.

67
00:02:55,080 --> 00:02:58,280
So many people have these in their cars these days.

68
00:02:58,280 --> 00:03:04,520
This is like an electronic map that will use your location to show you where to go.

69
00:03:05,140 --> 00:03:06,360
It's very useful.

70
00:03:06,360 --> 00:03:15,200
And especially in places like the United States that have streets that are clearly marked and it's just a little bit easier to get around.

71
00:03:15,930 --> 00:03:20,170
You can just get in your car, type in the address you want to go to and the thing talks to you.

72
00:03:20,840 --> 00:03:23,160
It says turn left, go straight, turn right.

73
00:03:23,160 --> 00:03:23,390
Creepy.

74
00:03:24,160 --> 00:03:26,600
So this is a very useful device.

75
00:03:26,600 --> 00:03:29,070
It's like a computer that you use in your computer, a GPS.

76
00:03:30,350 --> 00:03:38,490
All right, so she's talking about the GPS and then at the end of that line, she says, this is so typical.

77
00:03:39,440 --> 00:03:39,640
So what?

78
00:03:40,440 --> 00:03:41,440
Getting lost.

79
00:03:41,440 --> 00:03:43,720
All right, getting lost is so typical.

80
00:03:43,720 --> 00:03:46,480
So something that is typical is common.

81
00:03:47,680 --> 00:03:48,600
This is so normal.

82
00:03:48,960 --> 00:03:49,780
This is so typical.

83
00:03:50,020 --> 00:03:52,620
